  23:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****                       ##### WWDG Specific features #####
  24:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****   ==============================================================================
  25:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****   [..]
  26:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     Once enabled the WWDG generates a system reset on expiry of a programmed
  27:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     time period, unless the program refreshes the counter (T[6;0] downcounter)
  28:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     before reaching 0x3F value (i.e. a reset is generated when the counter
  29:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     value rolls down from 0x40 to 0x3F).
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccrQVJnq.s 			page 2


  30:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
  31:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) An MCU reset is also generated if the counter value is refreshed
  32:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         before the counter has reached the refresh window value. This
  33:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         implies that the counter must be refreshed in a limited window.
  34:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) Once enabled the WWDG cannot be disabled except by a system reset.
  35:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) If required by application, an Early Wakeup Interrupt can be triggered
  36:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         in order to be warned before WWDG expiration. The Early Wakeup Interrupt
  37:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (EWI) can be used if specific safety operations or data logging must
  38:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         be performed before the actual reset is generated. When the downcounter
  39:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         reaches 0x40, interrupt occurs. This mechanism requires WWDG interrupt
  40:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         line to be enabled in NVIC. Once enabled, EWI interrupt cannot be
  41:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         disabled except by a system reset.
  42:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) WWDGRST flag in RCC CSR register can be used to inform when a WWDG
  43:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         reset occurs.
  44:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) The WWDG counter input clock is derived from the APB clock divided
  45:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         by a programmable prescaler.
  46:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) WWDG clock (Hz) = PCLK1 / (4096 * Prescaler)
  47:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) WWDG timeout (mS) = 1000 * (T[5;0] + 1) / WWDG clock (Hz)
  48:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         where T[5;0] are the lowest 6 bits of Counter.
  49:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) WWDG Counter refresh is allowed between the following limits :
  50:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (++) min time (mS) = 1000 * (Counter - Window) / WWDG clock
  51:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (++) max time (mS) = 1000 * (Counter - 0x40) / WWDG clock
  52:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) Typical values:
  53:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (++) Counter min (T[5;0] = 0x00) at 170MHz (PCLK1) with zero prescaler:
  54:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****              max timeout before reset: approximately 24.09us
  55:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (++) Counter max (T[5;0] = 0x3F) at 170MHz (PCLK1) with prescaler
  56:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****              dividing by 128:
  57:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****              max timeout before reset: approximately 197.38ms
  58:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
  59:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  60:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****   ==============================================================================
  61:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
  62:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     *** Common driver usage ***
  63:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     ===========================
  64:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
  65:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****   [..]
  66:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) Enable WWDG APB1 clock using __HAL_RCC_WWDG_CLK_ENABLE().
  67:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) Configure the WWDG prescaler, refresh window value, counter value and early
  68:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         interrupt status using HAL_WWDG_Init() function. This will automatically
  69:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         enable WWDG and start its downcounter. Time reference can be taken from
  70:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         function exit. Care must be taken to provide a counter value
  71:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         greater than 0x40 to prevent generation of immediate reset.
  72:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) If the Early Wakeup Interrupt (EWI) feature is enabled, an interrupt is
  73:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         generated when the counter reaches 0x40. When HAL_WWDG_IRQHandler is
  74:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         triggered by the interrupt service routine, flag will be automatically
  75:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         cleared and HAL_WWDG_WakeupCallback user callback will be executed. User
  76:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         can add his own code by customization of callback HAL_WWDG_WakeupCallback.
  77:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) Then the application program must refresh the WWDG counter at regular
  78:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         intervals during normal operation to prevent an MCU reset, using
  79:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         HAL_WWDG_Refresh() function. This operation must occur only when
  80:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         the counter is lower than the refresh window value already programmed.
  81:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
  82:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     *** Callback registration ***
  83:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     =============================
  84:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
  85:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****   [..]
  86:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     The compilation define USE_HAL_WWDG_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1 allows
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccrQVJnq.s 			page 3


  87:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks. Use Functions
  88:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     HAL_WWDG_RegisterCallback() to register a user callback.
  89:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
  90:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) Function HAL_WWDG_RegisterCallback() allows to register following
  91:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         callbacks:
  92:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (++) EwiCallback : callback for Early WakeUp Interrupt.
  93:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (++) MspInitCallback : WWDG MspInit.
  94:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
  95:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     and a pointer to the user callback function.
  96:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
  97:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     (+) Use function HAL_WWDG_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to
  98:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     the default weak (surcharged) function. HAL_WWDG_UnRegisterCallback()
  99:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle and the Callback ID.
 100:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 101:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (++) EwiCallback : callback for  Early WakeUp Interrupt.
 102:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****         (++) MspInitCallback : WWDG MspInit.
 103:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
 104:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     [..]
 105:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     When calling HAL_WWDG_Init function, callbacks are reset to the
 106:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     corresponding legacy weak (surcharged) functions:
 107:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     HAL_WWDG_EarlyWakeupCallback() and HAL_WWDG_MspInit() only if they have
 108:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     not been registered before.
 109:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c **** 
 110:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     [..]
 111:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     When compilation define USE_HAL_WWDG_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 112:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     not defined, the callback registering feature is not available
 113:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_wwdg.c ****     and weak (surcharged) callbacks are used.
